      "value": "@{5b08f077c047d9049827e1c3|full_name}: I'm not sure where you're getting your info but you're flat out wrong on multiple levels. No one is being forced to upvote this.\nIn any discord I tried to get to signal boost the post I  included what was affected not to mention the poster clarified in a comment with exmaples. If you're talking about people spawning cameras that you can move around and replacing people's viewpoints when you reference terror, that's unrelated to this and is an entirely separate security issue altogether. Very few people actually knew about and were actively abusing the unity cameras we use for our effects. Many things are used in ways that they aren't intended for already and it's because of this continued openness and discovery that we've seen some of the most incredible things in this game. Adding every single person that you want to see your effect you worked hard on is terribly inconvenient. Not all of us want every single person in any given lobby on our friends list just so they can see something we've created for other's enjoyment. If we'd \"rampage\" over the option we're literally asking for then we wouldn't ask for this compromise at all we'd ask for the cameras to be made identical to how they once were. I recommend looking into what's actually affected and reevaluating your sources when it comes to the supposed issues unity cameras are causing because I think you'll find a lot of it is unrelated. In the event that this feature is recognized and integrated into the menu like we're requesting, you can pay the 100 bucks you owe us for that bet starting here: https://paypal.me/MBrero\nIf you still think you're right that is.\n\n;)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
